### List calendar events (first page, default sort)
# Prereqs:
# - Azurite running and the Azure Functions host started.
# - The `local` environment is selected in the Visual Studio HTTP editor.
# - `accessToken` is set in `http-client.env.json.user` (not committed).
#   See docs/api/development/build-and-test.md, "Acquiring a development
#   access token".
# - Create at least one calendar event first if a non-empty response is needed.
# Expected response: 200 OK with a paged envelope
# { items, page, pageSize, totalCount, sort, direction }. With no query the API
# defaults to page 0, pageSize 10, sort scheduledStart, direction desc.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### List calendar events with explicit paging and sort
# Expected response: 200 OK. Sortable fields are scheduledStart, timeZone, and
# title; direction is asc or desc.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events?page=0&pageSize=10&sort=scheduledStart&direction=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### List calendar events sorted by title ascending
# Expected response: 200 OK ordered by the English title, then calendar event id
# ascending.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events?sort=title&direction=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get a single calendar event by id
# Replace the id with one returned by a list call. The response item has the
# same shape as a list item (local start, time zone, descriptions).
# Expected response: 200 OK, or 404 Not Found for an unknown id.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events/REPLACE_WITH_CALENDAR_EVENT_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### List calendar events scoped to a local month (optional filter)
# Expected response: 200 OK with only that local month's events. year and month
# are optional but must be supplied together.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events?year=2026&month=6
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Second page
# Expected response: 200 OK with items[] for page index 1 (empty when there are
# 10 or fewer events), and totalCount reflecting all events.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Invalid pageSize
# Expected response: 400 Bad Request (pageSize must be between 1 and 100).

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events?pageSize=0
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Invalid sort field
# Expected response: 400 Bad Request (sort must be scheduledStart, timeZone, or
# title).

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events?sort=descriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Year without month
# Expected response: 400 Bad Request (year and month must be provided together).

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events?year=2026
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Invalid month with year
# Expected response: 400 Bad Request (validation rejects month 13).

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events?year=2026&month=13
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Missing bearer token
# Expected response: 401 Unauthorized with an empty body
# (BearerTokenMiddleware short-circuits on AuthenticateAsync failure).

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events

### Invalid bearer token
# Expected response: 401 Unauthorized.
# Any non-JWT or wrong-signature token fails signature/issuer validation.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events
Authorization: Bearer not-a-jwt

### Read endpoint with a write-only token
# Optional: paste a token that only carries the `CalendarEvents.Write`
# scope into `accessTokenWriteOnly` (set in `http-client.env.json.user`).
# Expected response: 403 Forbidden (AuthorizationMiddleware short-circuits
# when the required `CalendarEvents.Read` scope is absent).
# Skip this request if a write-only token is not available.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessTokenWriteOnly}}
